Theorem TF-11: Standard backward demand + raw-before-observation seq_add soundness

  Preconditions:
    - TF-11 backward demand emits `(operand, cardinality=Once, consumption=Linear)`
      per operand of each ArcInstr per Annex E §AIMS TF-11
    - `consumption=Linear` is load-bearing: without it CN-1 (Dead ↔ Absent)
      erases the demand. Per Annex E §AIMS TF-11 statement.
    - Per-variable demand from MULTIPLE instructions ADDITIVELY combines via
      `seq_add` over Cardinality x Consumption — NOT lattice `max`
    - Consumption `seq_add` matrix per Annex E §AIMS TF-11:
        Dead + X = X
        Linear + Linear = Unrestricted
        Linear + Affine = Unrestricted
        Affine + Affine = Unrestricted
        X + Unrestricted = Unrestricted
    - Per-Instr demand patterns enumerated verbatim from Annex E §AIMS TF-11
      table (Let / Construct / Project / Apply / ApplyIndirect / Set / SetTag /
      IsShared / Reset / Reuse / CollectionReuse / Select / RcInc / RcDec)
    - IA-5 step (1) alias transfers use `seq_add` per Annex E §AIMS IA-5;
      cross-instruction accumulation soundness MUST hold uniformly
    - Cardinality and Consumption remain independent `RawDemand` evidence
      throughout a block's backward fold; CN-1 canonicalization runs once at
      the observation boundary, not after each individual contribution
    - A Project contributes fixed Affine Consumption even when its destination
      Cardinality is Absent; a lone such contribution canonicalizes to Dead,
      but its Affine evidence must compose with any other demand first

  Soundness property:
    Forall arc_instr in ArcInstr.
      backward_demand_tf11(arc_instr) = expected per the §3 TF-11 table row
      AND seq_add: Consumption x Consumption -> Consumption is sound per the
      4 x 4 = 16 input matrix verbatim from Annex E §AIMS TF-11
      AND seq_add restricted to Cardinality x Cardinality is sound per the
      3 x 3 = 9 input matrix derived from §1.3 (Absent + X = X; Once + Once =
      Many; X + Many = Many)
    AND L-6 monotonicity: a1 <=_C a2 implies seq_add(a1, c) <=_C seq_add(a2, c)
    for fixed c (`seq_add` monotone in each argument per §1.2 / §1.3 lattice
    properties)
    AND RawDemand.seqAdd is associative and commutative, imperative left-fold
    accumulation equals the declarative raw sum, and every permutation has the
    same raw result before observation
    AND eager CN-1 observation is rejected by the concrete
    `(Absent, Affine) + (Once, Linear)` witness: eager observation produces
    `(Once, Linear)`, while raw fold then one observation produces
    `(Once, Unrestricted)`
    AND a lone `(Absent, Affine)` Project contribution observes as
    `(Absent, Dead)`.

  Proof obligation:
    Five-part discharge:
      (a) Per-Instr demand-table enumeration — 14 instructions per §3 TF-11
          table; each row's demand list verified against the §3 statement.
      (b) Consumption `seq_add` 4 x 4 matrix enumeration — 16 inputs;
          each row verified against the 5-rule statement.
      (c) Cardinality `seq_add` 3 x 3 matrix enumeration — 9 inputs;
          (Absent absorbing on left; Once + Once = Many; Many absorbing).
      (d) Monotonicity check — `seq_add` monotone in argument 1 over the
          Consumption lattice (Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted per
          §1.2) AND over the Cardinality lattice (Absent < Once < Many
          per §1.3).
      (e) Raw-demand timing — prove associativity, commutativity, left-fold /
          right-fold equality, and permutation invariance before observation;
          prove the eager-CN-1 non-commutation witness and both required final
          observations under the existing canonicalize definition.

    Part (a) — per-Instr demand-table enumeration:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-11 table:
        Let { Var(v) } -> NONE (transparent alias; IA-5 transfers)
        Let { Literal } -> none
        Let { PrimOp { args } } -> (arg, Once) per arg
        Construct { args } -> (arg, Once) per arg
        Project { value } -> NONE (borrow; IA-5 / TF-14)
        Apply { args } -> (arg, Once, Linear) per arg (IC-3)
        ApplyIndirect { closure, args } -> (closure, Once), (arg, Once)/arg
        Set { base, field, value } -> (base, Once) + (value, Once, Linear)
        SetTag { base, tag } -> (base, Once) only
        IsShared { var } -> (var, Once)
        Reset { var } -> (var, Once)
        Reuse { token, args } -> (token, Once) + (arg, Once)/arg
        CollectionReuse { old, args}-> (old, Once) + (arg, Once)/arg
        Select { cond, t, f } -> (cond, Once) only (IA-5 transfers t/f)
        RcInc/RcDec { var } -> none (RC op, not a use)
      Verified: backward_demand_tf11_lookup() enumerates every row above
      EXACTLY and produces the demand list verbatim. 14-row table is closed
      (no missing instruction).

    Part (b) — Consumption seq_add 4 x 4 matrix:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-11 `seq_add` matrix statement:
        seq_add(Dead, X) = X for all X
        seq_add(Linear, Linear) = Unrestricted
        seq_add(Linear, Affine) = Unrestricted
        seq_add(Affine, Linear) = Unrestricted (commutative — §1.2)
        seq_add(Affine, Affine) = Unrestricted
        seq_add(X, Unrestricted) = Unrestricted for all X
        seq_add(Unrestricted, X) = Unrestricted for all X
      Verified: seq_add_consumption(a, b) enumerates all 16 (a, b) pairs over
      {Dead, Linear, Affine, Unrestricted} x {Dead, Linear, Affine, Unrestricted}
      and matches the matrix.

    Part (c) — Cardinality seq_add 3 x 3 matrix:
      Per Annex E §AIMS + §3 TF-11 accumulation:
        seq_add(Absent, X) = X (Absent is the identity on the left)
        seq_add(Once, Once) = Many
        seq_add(Once, Many) = Many
        seq_add(Many, X) = Many
      Verified: seq_add_cardinality(a, b) enumerates all 9 (a, b) pairs over
      {Absent, Once, Many} x {Absent, Once, Many} and matches.

    Part (d) — monotonicity of seq_add:
      L-6 layer (b) for backward-demand accumulation:
        forall a1, a2, c in Consumption.
          a1 <=_C a2 implies seq_add(a1, c) <=_C seq_add(a2, c)
      Verified by exhaustive enumeration of the Consumption lattice
      (Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted): pick c in {Dead, Linear,
      Affine, Unrestricted}; for each pair (a1, a2) with a1 <= a2, verify
      seq_add(a1, c) <= seq_add(a2, c).
      Analogously for Cardinality lattice (Absent < Once < Many): 3 x 3 x 3
      = 27 monotonicity checks; all pass since seq_add is monotone on each
      argument per §1.2 + §1.3.

    Part (e) — raw demand algebra and observation timing:
      Define RawDemand as the backend-neutral product of independent
      Cardinality and Consumption evidence. Its `seqAdd` is componentwise and
      never invokes canonicalize. Its identity is `(Absent, Dead)`.
      Prove:
        RawDemand.seqAdd is associative and commutative.
        foldl(seqAdd, initial, demands) = seqAdd(initial, raw_sum(demands)).
        Perm(left, right) implies raw_sum(left) = raw_sum(right) before any
          observation.
      Define observe by embedding the raw pair in neutral AimsState dimensions,
      invoking the existing canonicalize definition once, then projecting the
      pair. This keeps CN-1's implementation single-sourced.
      Concrete negative witness:
        observe(seqAdd(observe(Absent, Affine), (Once, Linear)))
          = (Once, Linear)
        observe(seqAdd((Absent, Affine), (Once, Linear)))
          = (Once, Unrestricted)
        therefore eager observation does not commute with seqAdd.
      Concrete dead-only witness:
        observe(raw_sum([(Absent, Affine)])) = (Absent, Dead).
      Kernel discharge: AimsProof.Transfer.TF11_raw_demand_timing_sound;
      supporting theorems include RawDemand.sum_perm,
      RawDemand.eager_observation_yields_once_linear,
      RawDemand.eager_CN1_observation_does_not_commute_with_seqAdd,
      RawDemand.raw_fold_then_observe_once_unrestricted, and
      RawDemand.lone_dead_projection_observes_dead.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — seq_add monotonicity over Consumption + Cardinality
        lattices per section_04::verify_tf11_backward_demand_seq_add)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — 14-row per-Instr demand-table enumeration +
        16-entry Consumption matrix + 9-entry Cardinality matrix per
        section_04::verify_tf11_backward_demand_seq_add)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; matrix verification + lattice
        order consumed)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-11 emits no refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-11 matrices and the compiled Lean proves the raw-demand algebra, permutation invariance, and observe-once timing witnesses
